nested_fn_syntax.al:3:5: error: `inline` applies to top-level functions only: a nested function is declared as `name :: (a: A) -> R { ... }`
nested_fn_syntax.al:4:5: error: `noinline` applies to top-level functions only: a nested function is declared as `name :: (a: A) -> R { ... }`
nested_fn_syntax.al:5:5: error: `priv` applies to top-level declarations only; a local declaration is visible only in its block anyway, found keyword `priv`
nested_fn_syntax.al:6:5: error: `extern` applies to top-level functions only: a nested function is declared as `name :: (a: A) -> R { ... }`
nested_fn_syntax.al:7:10: error: an anonymous function cannot have type parameters of its own (it may use the type parameters of the enclosing function): write `(a: T) -> R { ... }`, or declare a generic function at the top level
nested_fn_syntax.al:8:10: error: an anonymous function names its parameters and gives each one a type, like any function: `(a: i64, b: i64) -> bool { a < b }` (`(A, B) -> R` alone is a function type)
nested_fn_syntax.al:9:5: error: inside a function only functions can be declared with `::` (`K :: (a: A) -> R { ... }`): a constant is declared at the top level
nested_fn_syntax.al:10:13: error: a constant is declared at the top level (`L : i64 : value` outside the function); a variable is `L: i64 = value`
nested_fn_syntax.al:11:5: error: inside a function only functions can be declared with `::` (`P :: (a: A) -> R { ... }`): a struct is declared at the top level
